<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? — 为什么天空是蓝色的？</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f7f9fc;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --text: #1f2937;
    --muted: #6b7280;
    --accent: #2563eb;
    --accent-soft: #e3edff;
    --border: #e5e7eb;
    --formula-bg: #f1f5f9;
    --shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  }
  [data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg: #0f172a;
    --surface: #1e293b;
    --text: #e5e7eb;
    --muted: #94a3b8;
    --accent: #60a5fa;
    --accent-soft: #1e3a5f;
    --border: #334155;
    --formula-bg: #0b1220;
    --shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", "PingFang SC", "Hiragino Sans GB", "Microsoft YaHei", Roboto, sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.7;
    transition: background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
  }
  header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #60a5fa 0%, #3b82f6 45%, #2563eb 100%);
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 2.5rem;
  }
  header .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  header h1 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.25; }
  header h2 { font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.6vw, 1.5rem); font-weight: 600; opacity: 0.95; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  header p { max-width: 640px; margin: 1.2rem auto 0; opacity: 0.9; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .toolbar {
    display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1rem 0;
  }
  .toolbar button {
    font: inherit; cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--surface); color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.45rem 1.1rem; font-size: 0.9rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  }
  .toolbar button:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); background: var(--accent-soft); }
  main { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 3rem; }
  section.level { margin-top: 2rem; }
  section.level > h2 {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  section.level > h2 .icon { font-size: 1.6rem; }
  section.level > h2 .zh { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; font-size: 1rem; }
  .columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .col {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .col .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .col p { margin-bottom: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.98rem; }
  .col p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .col strong { color: var(--accent); }
  .formula {
    background: var(--formula-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    margin: 0.9rem 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-family: "Cambria Math", Georgia, serif;
  }
  .formula small { display: block; font-family: inherit; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  footer { text-align: center; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; padding: 0 1rem 2.5rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="eyebrow">Bilingual / 双语</div>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?</h1>
  <h2>为什么天空是蓝色的？</h2>
  <p>Three explanations for three audiences — 三种受众、三种讲法</p>
</header>

<div class="toolbar">
  <button id="theme-toggle" type="button">🌙 Dark mode</button>
  <button id="top-button" type="button">↑ Top</button>
</div>

<main>

  <!-- 1. Toddler -->
  <section class="level" id="toddler">
    <h2><span class="icon">🎈</span> For a 3-Year-Old Toddler <span class="zh">对 3 岁幼儿</span></h2>
    <div class="columns">
      <article class="col">
        <span class="tag">English</span>
        <p>Look up! The sky is full of tiny air particles. Sunlight is a piece of light that changes into many colors — like a rainbow — when it goes through a prism.</p>
        <p>The tiny air particles in the sky bounce the light around, but they bounce the <strong>blue</strong> color bouncing around a lot more — just like a ball bouncing in a room!</p>
        <p>So when you look at the sky, all those bounced blue lights come to your eyes. That's why the sky looks blue! At sunrise or sunset, the sunlight travels through more air, and the blue color gets tired and doesn't reach you as well — that's why the sky turns pink and orange then.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="col">
        <span class="tag">中文</span>
        <p>抬头看！天空里有很多小空气粒子。阳光像一片会变成很多颜色的光——就像经过棱镜时会变成彩虹一样。</p>
        <p>天空里的小空气粒子会把光“弹”来“弹”去，但它们弹开<strong>蓝色</strong>的光得更多——就像房间里的球弹来弹去一样！</p>
        <p>所以，当你看天空时，所有被弹出的蓝色光都会射进你的眼睛。这就是天空看起来是蓝色的原因！在早晨或傍晚，阳光穿过更厚的空气，蓝色的光变得“累”了，没那么多能到达你这里——所以天空此时就会变成粉色和橙色。</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. High school teenager -->
  <section class="level" id="teen">
    <h2><span class="icon">🎓</span> For a High School Teenager <span class="zh">对高中学生</span></h2>
    <div class="columns">
      <article class="col">
        <span class="tag">English</span>
        <p>The sky is blue because of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>. Sunlight is made up of many colors (wavelengths). As it passes through Earth's atmosphere, it bumps into tiny gas molecules — mostly nitrogen and oxygen — that are much smaller than the wavelengths of visible light.</p>
        <p>When light scatters in this small-particle regime, the scattering efficiency depends on wavelength: it goes as 1/λ⁴. Blue light (~450 nm) is scattered roughly 4–5 times more strongly than red light (~700 nm). As sunlight enters the atmosphere, much of its blue light gets scattered sideways in all directions. Your eyes — and the sky itself — pick up this scattered blue light from every part of the sky, giving it that blue color.</p>
        <p>At sunrise or sunset, sunlight travels through much more of the atmosphere, so the blue is scattered away before it reaches you; only the longer-wavelength red and orange light gets through, which is why the sky glows orange and red then. (Fun fact: the sky is essentially the same blue everywhere — it's the scattered light filling all directions, not light coming from a "blue layer.")</p>
      </article>
      <article class="col">
        <span class="tag">中文</span>
        <p>天空呈蓝色，是因为<strong>瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）</strong>。阳光由许多颜色（波长）组成。当它穿过地球大气层时，会撞击很多比可见光波长小得多的小气体分子——主要是氮气和氧气。</p>
        <p>当光在这种小颗粒体系中散射时，散射效率取决于波长：它与 1/λ⁴ 成正比。蓝光（约 450 nm）比红光（约 700 nm）被散射得强约 4–5 倍。当阳光进入大气层时，其中很多蓝色光会被向四面八方散开。你的眼睛——以及天空本身——接收到来自各个方向的散射蓝光，于是天空就呈现出蓝色。</p>
        <p>在日出或日落时，阳光穿过更厚的大气层，蓝光在抵达你之前就被散射回去了，只有波长较长的红光和橙光能到达你，所以这时天空会呈现橙红色。（有趣的事实：天空到处大体上是同一个蓝色——这是散射光充满各个方向造成的，并不是来自一个“蓝色层”的光。）</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Physics PhD -->
  <section class="level" id="phd">
    <h2><span class="icon">⚛️</span> For a Physics PhD <span class="zh">对物理博士</span></h2>
    <div class="columns">
      <article class="col">
        <span class="tag">English</span>
        <p>The blue color of the sky arises from <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> of solar radiation by atmospheric molecules in the limit where the scatterer size (a) is much smaller than the wavelength of light (λ), i.e., ka ≪ 1. In this regime, the differential scattering cross-section for unpolarized light is:</p>
        <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = r₀² (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <p>where the Rayleigh scattering length is:</p>
        <div class="formula">r₀ ∝ λ⁻⁴ / (1 + 2cos²θ)</div>
        <p>More precisely, the total Rayleigh scattering cross-section for a single molecule scales as:</p>
        <div class="formula">σ<sub>Rayleigh</sub> = (8π⁴α²) / (3λ⁴)<small>α = molecular polarizability</small></div>
        <p>The key result is the λ⁻⁴ dependence: blue light (λ ≈ 450 nm) scatters about (700/450)⁴ ≈ 4.7 times more strongly than red light (λ ≈ 700 nm).</p>
        <p>Photometric integrals over the 4π solid angle, combined with the atmospheric molecular number density (n(h) ≈ n₀e<sup>–h/H</sup>, with scale height H ≈ 8 km), yield the total scattered-light intensity. The angular distribution of scattered intensity (1 + cos²θ)/2 leads to the classic sky-color distribution, with maximum intensity at 90° from the sun.</p>
        <p>The solar spectrum inside the atmosphere is depleted of short wavelengths, which is also why the sun appears white-ish in midday sky (direct sunlight is slightly yellowed by selective scattering of blue), and red-orange near the horizon at low solar elevation, where the air mass factor (AM ≈ 1/cos(zenith angle)) becomes large. At large AM, the direct beam is dominated by red/orange wavelengths, and scattered skylight becomes relatively orange-pink — the basis for sunset colors. Polarization of skylight also follows from Rayleigh scattering, giving linear polarization maximal at the 90° position relative to the sun.</p>
        <p>For completeness: aerosols in the troposphere cause Mie scattering (weak wavelength dependence, giving white/gray skies), and stratospheric ozone absorbs some UV/blue (Chappuis and Hartley bands), subtly modulating the perceived color. But the dominant mechanism for a clear-sky blue is molecular Rayleigh scattering.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="col">
        <span class="tag">中文</span>
        <p>天空呈蓝色，源于大气分子对太阳辐射的<strong>瑞利散射</strong>，在散射体尺寸（a）远小于光的波长（λ）的极限下，即 ka ≪ 1。在这个区域，非偏振光的微分散射截面为：</p>
        <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = r₀² (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <p>其中瑞利散射长度为：</p>
        <div class="formula">r₀ ∝ λ⁻⁴ / (1 + 2cos²θ)</div>
        <p>更精确地说，单个分子的总瑞利散射截面按下式缩放：</p>
        <div class="formula">σ<sub>Rayleigh</sub> = (8π⁴α²) / (3λ⁴)<small>α = 分子极化率</small></div>
        <p>关键结果是 λ⁻⁴ 依赖性：蓝光（λ ≈ 450 nm）比红光（λ ≈ 700 nm）被散射得强约 (700/450)⁴ ≈ 4.7 倍。</p>
        <p>对 4π 立体角进行光度积分，并结合大气分子数密度（n(h) ≈ n₀e<sup>–h/H</sup>，其中标高 H ≈ 8 km），可以得到总散射光强。散射光强的角分布（1 + cos²θ）/2 导致经典的天空颜色分布，在与太阳成 90° 处达到最大强度。</p>
        <p>因此太阳光谱在大气层内被短波长成分耗减，这也是中午太阳呈现白色偏黄的原因（直接阳光经部分蓝光散射后略微变黄），以及在低太阳高度角时近地平线太阳呈现红橙色的原因，此时空气质量因子（AM ≈ 1/cos(天顶角)）很大。在大 AM 时，直接光束由红橙色波长主导，散射天空光相对呈现橙粉色——这就是日落颜色的基础。天空光的偏振同样源于瑞利散射，在与太阳成 90° 处产生最大的线偏振。</p>
        <p>为完整起见：对流层中的气溶胶引起米氏散射（波长依赖性弱，形成白色/灰色天空），平流层臭氧吸收部分紫外和蓝光（Chappuis 带和 Hartley 带），微妙地调制了视觉感知的颜色。但清晰天空蓝色的主导机制仍是分子瑞利散射。</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer>
  <p>Why Is the Sky Blue? / 为什么天空是蓝色的？</p>
  <p>English &amp; 中文双语对照 · 无外部资源，全部内嵌</p>
</footer>

<script>
  (function () {
    var toggle = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
    var root = document.documentElement;
    function applyTheme(theme) {
      if (theme === 'dark') {
        root.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark');
        toggle.textContent = '☀️ Light mode';
      } else {
        root.removeAttribute('data-theme');
        toggle.textContent = '🌙 Dark mode';
      }
    }
    var saved = null;
    try { saved = localStorage.getItem('sky-theme'); } catch (e) {}
    if (saved) {
      applyTheme(saved);
    } else {
      try {
        if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches) {
          applyTheme('dark');
        }
      } catch (e) {}
    }
    toggle.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var isDark = root.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark';
      var next = isDark ? 'light' : 'dark';
      applyTheme(next);
      try { localStorage.setItem('sky-theme', next); } catch (e) {}
    });
    var top = document.getElementById('top-button');
    if (top) {
      top.addEventListener('click', function () {
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
      });
    }
  })();
</script>

</body>
</html>
